    "updated_at": "2022-03-26T22:40:44Z",
    "body": "Gotcha. Confirmed that it works on my copy of 0.11.0.\r\n\r\nI'm not familiar with the culture surrounding xonsh and upgrades: I know for both nushell and elvish, the creators explicitly say that things are expected to break between minor version releases and that you should always be running the most up-to-date shell (in the elvish community, there are modules which explicitly aren't guaranteed to work with anything but the HEAD version). Is xonsh similar, or is there a reasonable expectation at the moment that you can be e.g. 1 or 2 versions behind and still have working stuff?\r\n\r\nRight now, we don't explicitly have an earliest supported xonsh version, so if we wanted to make this change, we'd have to explicitly drop support for everything pre-0.11.0",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
