    "updated_at": "2022-03-27T11:52:07Z",
    "body": "Nope, sorry.  I realize I should have been more clear:\r\n\r\n* #3646 combined with the Starship standard instructions of `execx($(starship init xonsh))` does not support xonsh 0.11.0 and later since xonsh/xonsh/issues/3786 is now fixed.\r\n* xonsh users can use the `xontrib-prompt-starship` which does not use `execx($(starship init xonsh))` -- so #3646 doesn't impact those users. So, if you are (like me) starship users, find xonsh, install and you are blocked, you hit #3646.  If you're decently saavy, you quickly find the xontrib, and you're up and going.\r\n\r\nWhy don't you leave this open -- I think I can prototype the fix (check xonsh version and selectively add `| cat`).  I'll attach that here and that should make your decision on how to proceed easier.",
